{{night sky phone photography tips}}
find a dark spot away from streetlights. let your eyes adjust for 20 minutes. use a tripod or rest your phone on a stable surface. turn off flash and hdr. open night mode or pro mode. set iso to 800-3200 and shutter to 10-30 seconds. focus manually near infinity. use a 2-10 second timer to avoid shake. shoot in raw if your phone allows. use the widest lens and avoid digital zoom. turn screen brightness down after framing. use a star map app to find targets. try a new moon or crescent moon. include trees, rocks, or buildings for scale. take many frames and pick the sharpest. edit gently: lift shadows, lower noise, keep colors natural.
p.s. practice and patience matter more than gear.

